cff-version: 1.2.0

message: >-
  If you use PyAEZ in research, technical assessments, reports,
  publications, or derived software, please cite it using the
  metadata provided in this file.

title: "PyAEZ Version 3.0: A Modular Python Framework for Agro-Ecological Zoning"

type: software

version: "3.0.0-development"

date-released: 2026-MM-DD

authors:
  - name: "Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations"

abstract: >-
  PyAEZ is an open and modular Python implementation of the
  Agro-Ecological Zoning (AEZ) framework. It provides transparent,
  code-based workflows for climate-regime analysis, crop simulation,
  climatic-constraint assessment, soil and terrain evaluation, and
  agro-ecological suitability analysis. PyAEZ supports global,
  national, and subnational datasets, including soil, climate, crop,
  terrain, and user-defined scenario data.

keywords:
  - agro-ecological zoning
  - AEZ
  - crop suitability
  - land suitability
  - crop simulation
  - climate assessment
  - soil suitability
  - terrain constraints
  - attainable yield
  - geospatial analysis
  - Python
  - FAO

repository-code: "https://github.com/un-fao/pyaezv3/"

url: "https://github.com/un-fao/pyaez/"

